IMPORT `g8-fees`

-- ind-c-tests-fees.l4: independent tests (ind-c) of the Fees Regulations in three vintages.
-- Figures read from the sources: the SimpLEX draft from the screenshot (273, 194, 40, 284, 398); as made from
-- KT 11951 (194, 40, 284, 398); as amended from KT 12383 (adds 158; narrows the objection charge to the
-- theoretical exam).  Scenario ids are those of work/ind-c/expectations.md, section H and I.

§ `ind-c: the Fees Regulations`

§§ `Fixtures`

`draft` MEANS `the SimpLEX draft of the Fees Regulations`
`as made` MEANS `the Fees Regulations as made`
`as amended` MEANS `the Fees Regulations as amended`

-- Index readings: the June 2025 reading (the base of the first update, 1 January 2026: the index published in the
-- month before the commencement in July 2025), the November 2025 reading and the November 2026 reading.
GIVEN jun25 IS A NUMBER
      nov25 IS A NUMBER
      nov26 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Price index reading`
`ind-c readings` jun25 nov25 nov26 MEANS
    LIST (`Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 5, `published on` IS YMD 2025 6 15, `value of the index` IS jun25)
       , (`Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2025, `month of the index` IS 10, `published on` IS YMD 2025 11 14, `value of the index` IS nov25)
       , (`Price index reading` WITH `year of the index` IS 2026, `month of the index` IS 10, `published on` IS YMD 2026 11 13, `value of the index` IS nov26)

-- Flat readings: no change of the index, so every updated fee equals the printed one.
`flat readings` MEANS `ind-c readings` 100 100 100

§§ `H1-H8: the printed figure, per service and per vintage`

-- H1: a theoretical exam: draft 273; as made silent (never 273, never 158); as amended 158.
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` EQUALS JUST 273
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` EQUALS JUST 158
-- H2: a practical exam: 194 in all three.
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 194
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of sitting a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 194
-- H3: an objection to a practical-exam score: draft 40; as made 40; as amended silent.
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` EQUALS NOTHING
-- H4: an objection to a theoretical-exam score: draft 40; as amended 40 (as made is ambiguity X8: both readings below).
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` `the exam is the one exam the regulations define` `, for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT isJust (`the Fees Regulations as made state, reading "the exam" in regulation 2(b) as` `the exam is any exam` `, for the service` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam`)
-- H5: the licence (grant or renewal), as made and as amended: 284.  (The draft is in the ambiguous file: its 2(d)
-- prices "an application to receive a licence".)
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 284
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 284
-- H6: the foreign expert's temporary licence (application or renewal): 398 in all three.
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 398
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` EQUALS JUST 398
-- H7: a s.17 training course: silent in all three.
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of attending a continuing training course` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of attending a continuing training course` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of attending a continuing training course` EQUALS NOTHING
-- H8: a separate fee for filing an ordinary licence application: silent as made and as amended (the draft is in the
-- ambiguous file).  The grant of a temporary licence (as distinct from its application): silent in all three.
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of filing an application for a licence or its renewal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `draft` `for the service` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as made` `for the service` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the amount the Fees Regulations state in` `as amended` `for the service` `the service of being granted a foreign expert's temporary licence` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `H9: what an exam and its objections cost`

-- As amended, a theoretical exam with two objections: 158 + 2 x 40 = 238 in all; the objection charges alone 80.
#ASSERT `the printed amount due, reading the objection charge as` `the fee of the exam objected to and the objection charge` `, in` `as amended` `for the objection` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` `, the number of objections` 2 EQUALS JUST 238
#ASSERT `the printed amount due, reading the objection charge as` `the objection charge alone` `, in` `as amended` `for the objection` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` `, the number of objections` 2 EQUALS JUST 80
-- As made, a practical exam with one objection: 194 + 40 = 234.
#ASSERT `the printed amount due, reading the objection charge as` `the fee of the exam objected to and the objection charge` `, in` `as made` `for the objection` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` `, the number of objections` 1 EQUALS JUST 234
-- Draft, a theoretical exam with one appeal: 273 + 40 = 313.
#ASSERT `the printed amount due, reading the objection charge as` `the fee of the exam objected to and the objection charge` `, in` `draft` `for the objection` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` `, the number of objections` 1 EQUALS JUST 313

§§ `H10: which vintage is in force on a day`

#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS JUST `as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2026 5 3) EQUALS JUST `as made`
#ASSERT `the vintage of the Fees Regulations in force on` (YMD 2026 5 4) EQUALS JUST `as amended`
#ASSERT `the Fees Regulations as made came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
#ASSERT `the 2026 amendment of the Fees Regulations came into force on` EQUALS YMD 2026 5 4

§§ `I1-I5: regulation 3, the update, rounded to the nearest whole shekel`

-- I1: the licence fee on 2026-03-01 (as made), the index 100 (June 2025) -> 101.7 (November 2025): 288.828 -> 289.
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` `as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`ind-c readings` 100 101.7 101.7) EQUALS JUST 289
-- I2: the practical exam, 100 -> 103: 199.82 -> 200.
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` `as made` `the service of sitting a practical exam` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`ind-c readings` 100 103 103) EQUALS JUST 200
-- I3: the temporary licence, 100 -> 102.5: 407.95 -> 408.
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` `as made` `the service of filing an application for a foreign expert's temporary licence or its renewal` (YMD 2026 3 1) (`ind-c readings` 100 102.5 102.5) EQUALS JUST 408
-- I4: the theoretical exam fee 158, which took effect 2026-05-04, on 2027-02-01: the 1 January 2027 update by
-- November 2026 against November 2025 (102 -> 105.162, +3.1 per cent): 162.898 -> 163.  The 1 January 2026 update
-- (June 2025 100 -> November 2025 102) came before the fee existed and does not touch it.
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` `as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` (YMD 2027 2 1) (`ind-c readings` 100 102 105.162) EQUALS JUST 163
-- I5: before the first update day (1 January 2026) the printed figure, with no readings at all.
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` `as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` (YMD 2025 12 31) EMPTY EQUALS JUST 284
-- I5: the first update day after the commencement is 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the first update day after the commencement day` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 1
-- The first base index is the reading published in June 2025, the month before July 2025.
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — the calendar month before the month of` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS (`Calendar month under regulation 3` WITH `year of the calendar month` IS 2025, `number of the calendar month` IS 6)
-- Rounding to the whole shekel, not to NIS 10: 288.828 -> 289.
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — rounded to the nearest whole new shekel, a half shekel being treated by` `a half shekel is rounded up` `, the number` 288.828 EQUALS 289
-- A fee asked about before the vintage was in force: no fee under it.
#ASSERT `the fee under the Fees Regulations in the vintage for the service on the day` `as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` (YMD 2026 5 3) `flat readings` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `I6-I9: regulation 4, payment in full as a condition`

-- I6: the licence, as made, on 2025-08-01 (before any update): 283 paid: barred; 284: not barred; 300: not barred.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 283 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 284 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 300 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
-- I7: the practical exam: 193 barred, 194 not (as made; as amended on 2026-06-01 with a flat index, the same).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of sitting a practical exam` 193 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of sitting a practical exam` 194 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of sitting a practical exam` 193 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of sitting a practical exam` 194 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`
-- I8: the theoretical exam: as made no fee is fixed, so nothing paid is no bar; as amended 157 barred, 158 not, 0 barred.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 157 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 158 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of sitting a theoretical exam` 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`)
-- I9: an objection to a practical-exam score: as made 39 barred, 40 not; as amended no fee is fixed: 0 is no bar.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` 39 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` 40 (YMD 2025 8 1) EMPTY
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of objecting to the score of a practical exam` 0 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`
-- An objection to a theoretical-exam score as amended: 39 barred, 40 not.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` 39 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`)
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of objecting to the score of a theoretical exam` 40 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`
-- The licence as amended on 2026-06-01, flat index: 284 not barred, 283 barred.
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 284 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as amended` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 283 (YMD 2026 6 1) `flat readings`)
-- After the 2026 update (100 -> 101.7, 284 -> 289), 284 paid is no longer the fee in full.
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 284 (YMD 2026 3 1) (`ind-c readings` 100 101.7 101.7))
#ASSERT `regulation 4 does not bar the service in the vintage` `as made` `the service of receiving a licence or its renewal` 289 (YMD 2026 3 1) (`ind-c readings` 100 101.7 101.7)

§§ `X6: reg 3, a half shekel, both readings checked`

#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — rounded to the nearest whole new shekel, a half shekel being treated by` `a half shekel is rounded up` `, the number` 40.5 EQUALS 41
#ASSERT `regulation 3(a) — rounded to the nearest whole new shekel, a half shekel being treated by` `a half shekel is rounded to the even shekel` `, the number` 40.5 EQUALS 40
